"Nala is a woven transmigrator: neither born into a body nor put into a dead one."
"No body waited for her, so the System wove one whole at Greyfen Ford from her soul's own pattern."
"The weave took the shape her soul fit most easily, and that shape was a young human woman's."
"She was pulled out of a doze from an Earth the meteors had not yet reached."
"She came in the long tail of Earth's integration, after its wave had already landed."
"Her Starfall Legacy is the unspent integration of Earth souls lost before they could land."
"Those lost shares pooled in the one vessel the weave made, so her reserves run deep and refill."
"She holds all five elements attuned, which no human of this world is born holding."
"Low Analyze shows her as Human, Level 1; only high Analyze sees a legacy nobody has heard of."
"The Umarii Oracle sees her as a blank in the storm of futures, and it troubles her."
"The Verdant Empire's binder has no question fitting a transmigrator who arrived grown and whole."
"The legacy grows a rank when she overcomes a foe or feat far beyond her level with it."
